道行く人に元気にあいさつ

01:23.930 --> 01:30.470
Cheerfully greet people walking down the city streets

01:30.470 --> 01:37.110
atarashii kimochi de shinkokyuu shitara

01:30.470 --> 01:37.110
新しい 気持ちで　深呼吸したら

01:30.470 --> 01:37.110
Take a deep breath to refresh yourself

01:37.110 --> 01:45.610
kono sekai wa hora itsudemo kimi no mono

01:37.110 --> 01:45.610
この世界はほら、いつでも　君のもの

01:37.110 --> 01:45.610
And this world will always be yours

01:51.040 --> 02:00.960
Episode 11 :

01:51.040 --> 02:00.960
" Prayer "

02:01.100 --> 02:02.590
Hey, Yune-chan,

02:02.590 --> 02:04.010
why don't you come with me?

02:04.260 --> 02:06.990
The <i>Grand Magasin</i> is very fun!

02:06.990 --> 02:09.430
There's so many things to see!

02:09.430 --> 02:11.750
It's as if...

02:13.050 --> 02:15.640
Emptied a treasure chest...

02:15.640 --> 02:16.470
That's right!

02:16.470 --> 02:19.400
It's as if someone emptied a treasure chest on the floor!

02:21.280 --> 02:25.210
Also, by my elder brother's request, we're having a Japanese exhibition!

02:25.210 --> 02:26.990
I'm sure you'll love it!

02:29.590 --> 02:32.430
But Claude-sama is out, so...

02:32.430 --> 02:34.970
Don't worry about that guy!

02:34.970 --> 02:37.290
I can't do that!

02:40.060 --> 02:43.770
You really don't give up once you're like this, do you?

02:44.310 --> 02:45.560
I'm sorry.

02:45.560 --> 02:48.640
God! He's never here when he needs to be!

02:48.640 --> 02:50.140
Claude Claudel...!

02:51.290 --> 02:53.300
I'm very sorry.

02:53.300 --> 02:57.560
He left yesterday to deliver a sign to one of our regular customers.

02:57.960 --> 03:00.470
He should be back any time now.

03:00.950 --> 03:03.010
Oh, speak of the devil.

03:06.850 --> 03:08.700
Excellent timing!

03:08.700 --> 03:10.080
Wh-What the hell...?

03:10.080 --> 03:11.360
You're disturbing.

03:11.360 --> 03:12.830
Come on, Yune-chan!

03:15.800 --> 03:18.920
Don't you have something to ask him?

03:19.590 --> 03:20.830
Um...

03:20.830 --> 03:24.840
May I go to the <i>Grand Magasin</i> with Alice-sama?

03:26.300 --> 03:28.050
It's fine, right?

03:28.050 --> 03:33.110
I'd like to do everything Alice-sama wants me to do.

03:33.740 --> 03:38.070
Oh my, you're too cute!

03:40.940 --> 03:41.690
No.

03:42.950 --> 03:44.190
Claude-sama...

03:44.470 --> 03:46.690
The <i>Grand Magasin</i> is the <i>Galerie</i>'s enemy.

03:46.940 --> 03:49.900
You don't have to be that obstinate.

03:49.900 --> 03:51.960
Yune really wants to go, too.

03:51.960 --> 03:53.240
You've got to be kidding me.

03:53.240 --> 03:54.450
You're never going.

03:55.280 --> 03:57.660
You're still fussing over such a small...

04:00.700 --> 04:01.330
What?

04:01.820 --> 04:04.170
It's not like I asked <i>you</i> to come.

04:09.190 --> 04:11.010
I'm sorry, Yune-chan.

04:11.010 --> 04:12.690
I'll visit some other time.

04:12.690 --> 04:14.430
Alice-sama...

04:16.360 --> 04:17.940
Please excuse us.

04:25.660 --> 04:28.150
Did the deal go badly?

04:28.150 --> 04:29.440
No.

04:30.910 --> 04:34.410
Zidler-san always liked Jean,

04:34.690 --> 04:37.130
and you probably expected this to happen, anyway.

04:38.870 --> 04:41.750
He purchased the sign.

04:42.000 --> 04:43.860
He paid pretty well, too,

04:43.860 --> 04:46.920
which means he probably liked it.

04:47.670 --> 04:49.100
Then why don't you let-

04:49.100 --> 04:51.880
Oscar-sama, it's fine.

05:00.990 --> 05:02.100
Oscar-sama,

05:03.630 --> 05:08.770
does Claude-sama dislike the <i>Grand Magasin</i> not only because they are enemies,

05:08.770 --> 05:11.320
but for another reason?

05:14.270 --> 05:15.520
Does it...

05:17.040 --> 05:22.160
have something to do with Claude-sama's father?

05:25.710 --> 05:28.170
You've got some sharp intuition.

05:28.170 --> 05:31.270
He's just being a little sensitive.

05:32.020 --> 05:34.090
It's not something you should worry about.

06:05.860 --> 06:07.000
What is it?

06:07.690 --> 06:11.140
I've changed my mind.

06:11.140 --> 06:14.470
I don't want to go to the <i>Grand Magasin</i>.

06:15.880 --> 06:17.160
Why not?

06:17.160 --> 06:19.260
You looked so excited just a minute ago.

06:19.260 --> 06:20.610
I'm serious!

06:20.610 --> 06:23.100
I really don't want to go!

06:32.020 --> 06:32.990
Oh, really?

06:32.990 --> 06:34.080
That's good.

06:34.940 --> 06:37.030
I can concentrate on work now.

06:40.690 --> 06:44.340
Oh, right. Is there anywhere else that you want to go?

06:45.390 --> 06:47.870
A picnic at the park sounds nice.

06:47.870 --> 06:50.670
We'll take Grandpa and bring some lunch.

06:51.180 --> 06:52.210
How's that sound?

06:52.430 --> 06:54.560
I'd love to go!

06:57.170 --> 06:58.890
Are you fine with this?

06:59.250 --> 07:00.340
With what?

07:00.680 --> 07:03.530
Shouldn't you tell her?

07:03.530 --> 07:05.200
If you don't, Yune might-

07:05.200 --> 07:09.480
Nothing would change if I told her.

07:10.510 --> 07:13.440
Are you going to ignore Yune's feelings, too?

07:15.410 --> 07:19.010
Whether Yune is being honest or not,

07:19.010 --> 07:21.390
what's important will always be the same.

07:21.940 --> 07:24.830
She'd never lie with ill intent.

07:25.640 --> 07:29.610
She would never think of anything that would harm us.

07:31.180 --> 07:33.350
That much, I'm sure of.

07:33.350 --> 07:35.040
That's good enough.

07:35.880 --> 07:37.600
<i>You must trust her.</i>

07:38.390 --> 07:42.550
That's right. I can't do anything but trust her.

07:42.820 --> 07:47.770
<i>I like that part of you, but it's a bit cruel.</i>

07:52.090 --> 07:55.650
<i>Ever since Grandpa brought Yune here,</i>

07:55.650 --> 07:59.970
<i>I've been recalling all of these awful memories.</i>

07:59.970 --> 08:03.780
<i>Yune might already be aware of that.</i>

08:07.990 --> 08:11.580
<i>That's even less to worry about, then.</i>

08:12.220 --> 08:15.210
<i>She isn't a bad kid.</i>

08:15.880 --> 08:17.790
<i>I just have to be more relaxed.</i>

08:28.510 --> 08:30.310
It's so loud...

08:31.000 --> 08:34.310
I guess we can't have our picnic today.

08:34.310 --> 08:38.320
Don't worry, I'll stop the rain.

08:39.870 --> 08:41.930
I'll do it just for you!

08:47.250 --> 08:49.660
You really did stop the rain!

08:49.660 --> 08:52.970
You really <i>are</i> a magician, Oscar-sama!

08:54.980 --> 08:57.890
I told you, it doesn't rain for long in Paris.

08:57.890 --> 09:01.970
It doesn't matter, as long as she's happy.

09:02.430 --> 09:04.180
I'm quite honored.

09:22.690 --> 09:23.530
Wait up!

09:31.800 --> 09:33.540
Are you all right?

09:36.420 --> 09:38.920
Hey! There won't be anything left for you!

09:39.970 --> 09:40.670
Coming!

09:42.450 --> 09:43.000
Huh?

09:43.440 --> 09:44.620
It's empty.

09:48.720 --> 09:50.190
You did this!

09:51.770 --> 09:55.520
Sadly, Claude ate all of it, but...

09:57.160 --> 09:59.370
Just leave it to me...

10:02.790 --> 10:04.070
See?

10:05.530 --> 10:07.320
That's amazing!

10:13.210 --> 10:15.300
You take such small bites.

10:15.850 --> 10:16.920
Here, Yune.

10:17.850 --> 10:19.920
Next is an elixir.

10:20.470 --> 10:22.330
Thank you.

10:25.500 --> 10:26.660
It's very good.

10:26.660 --> 10:29.450
Is it? That's good, then.

10:48.620 --> 10:50.910
Hey, look, Claude.

10:52.760 --> 10:54.410
She's so carefree.

10:56.520 --> 10:57.700
Hey...

10:57.700 --> 11:00.680
Oscar-sama's magic...

11:01.540 --> 11:02.590
Is she...

11:02.590 --> 11:04.570
drunk...?

11:05.040 --> 11:06.600
This was unexpected...

11:06.600 --> 11:08.500
It was just a drop...

11:08.500 --> 11:09.780
Grandpa!

11:09.780 --> 11:14.310
I heard that Japanese people like to have banquets outdoors.

11:14.310 --> 11:17.580
I went to <i>hanami</i> with my sister!

11:14.310 --> 11:17.580
Hanami: Cherry blossom viewing + food + tons of alcohol.

11:17.580 --> 11:22.020
She was very pretty, just like Claude-sama!

11:22.020 --> 11:24.690
It's really affecting her.

11:27.840 --> 11:30.200
Shione... nee-sama...

11:32.370 --> 11:35.260
She must miss Japan.

11:36.230 --> 11:37.760
I'll go buy some water.

11:57.990 --> 12:00.340
I don't have any elixir...

12:00.340 --> 12:01.900
You've had enough.

12:12.350 --> 12:14.240
What are you doing?

12:38.730 --> 12:40.190
What was that?

12:40.190 --> 12:43.850
I greeted Paris' god for the first time.

12:44.370 --> 12:46.190
Paris' god...?

12:46.910 --> 12:49.360
Is he limited to only Paris?

12:49.360 --> 12:50.930
Is he not?!

12:51.410 --> 12:55.320
Then... he didn't hear my wish...

12:55.700 --> 12:57.420
Your wish?

12:57.420 --> 12:59.830
Oh? What'd you wish for?

13:01.120 --> 13:03.830
I'm sorry... it was about my home...

13:03.830 --> 13:05.420
Your home?

13:05.420 --> 13:07.380
That isn't anything to be ashamed of.

13:07.980 --> 13:10.600
About... my sister...

13:12.130 --> 13:16.970
That she would get better...

13:17.730 --> 13:19.640
She is...

13:20.360 --> 13:22.760
Sorry.

13:22.760 --> 13:24.350
You don't want to say it, do you?

13:28.550 --> 13:30.030
I won't ask.

13:36.990 --> 13:38.240
Is it raining again?

13:49.070 --> 13:49.960
Hey!

13:50.420 --> 13:52.150
I got some water!

14:01.540 --> 14:04.730
Are you all right now, Yune?

14:05.010 --> 14:05.850
Yes.

14:06.670 --> 14:08.590
Are you sure?

14:08.590 --> 14:09.520
Just now...

14:11.230 --> 14:12.640
what happened?

14:13.710 --> 14:15.650
Was it about your sister?

14:16.650 --> 14:20.830
I thought you said you didn't need details?

14:21.090 --> 14:22.480
I want to know.

14:23.090 --> 14:24.330
Please tell me.

14:28.740 --> 14:33.340
When I was young, she granted my wish.

14:34.460 --> 14:39.890
My sister actually became blind...

14:41.520 --> 14:48.780
She was not normal, because her eyes were just like Claude-sama's...

14:48.780 --> 14:51.470
Pale, sea-blue eyes.

14:54.370 --> 14:58.670
Everyone fears anything that isn't normal.

14:59.580 --> 15:04.180
I stole the light from my sister!

15:04.180 --> 15:06.660
I weakened my sister...

15:08.940 --> 15:13.060
Before then, I was much more sickly,

15:13.060 --> 15:17.740
and my sister always looked after me...

15:19.050 --> 15:21.470
But, one day...

15:22.070 --> 15:24.640
Shione-neesama?

15:25.290 --> 15:28.850
I don't want to see anyone's face anymore.

15:30.720 --> 15:33.000
When I open these eyes,

15:33.000 --> 15:37.620
all I can see are fading smiles.

15:39.150 --> 15:41.040
I see only those...

15:47.780 --> 15:49.720
Don't look at her.

15:51.280 --> 15:53.560
That's good to hear!

15:56.920 --> 15:58.010
How ominous...

15:58.480 --> 16:00.040
It's so creepy.

16:02.080 --> 16:06.790
I'm sure these eyes just bring misfortune.

16:06.790 --> 16:09.850
Your eyes are very pretty, though.

16:11.760 --> 16:14.430
You're the only one who says that.

16:18.770 --> 16:22.590
Only look at me, then!

16:28.450 --> 16:29.540
There!

16:29.880 --> 16:31.220
I cast a spell!

16:31.220 --> 16:33.500
You only have to see me,

16:33.870 --> 16:37.830
and no more scary faces.

16:41.550 --> 16:46.260
Since that day, we kept a secret.

16:47.220 --> 16:51.120
My sister pretended to be blind.

16:55.340 --> 16:56.360
Nee-sama.

16:58.970 --> 17:02.780
Only I could see my sister's eyes.

17:03.950 --> 17:08.040
But, after that I became much healthier,

17:08.040 --> 17:09.950
and my sister became much more sickly.

17:09.950 --> 17:11.040
Nee-sama?

17:12.090 --> 17:17.540
It really seems like I can only see you these days.

17:18.630 --> 17:21.400
Everything else is very fuzzy.

17:21.400 --> 17:22.300
Nee-sama...!

17:24.950 --> 17:26.610
It's fine.

17:26.610 --> 17:31.100
I'm much happier that way.

17:34.790 --> 17:39.780
Soon, my sister became completely blind...

17:43.030 --> 17:47.150
What's wrong? You were thinking only of your sister when you said that.

17:47.150 --> 17:50.290
Your sister just took you too seriously,

17:50.680 --> 17:52.250
and the blindness was just a coincidence.

17:57.900 --> 18:03.570
You know, your sister told me that story too.

18:03.570 --> 18:05.430
Even though she can't see,

18:05.430 --> 18:08.050
your words are her one and only light.

18:09.170 --> 18:11.730
She's just lying.

18:11.730 --> 18:14.110
She is very kind...

18:14.110 --> 18:18.480
You must think that you stole your sister's health and vision.

18:20.320 --> 18:25.510
Indeed, your words may have held some magical strength.

18:27.760 --> 18:30.120
<i>You only have to see me.</i>

18:31.220 --> 18:34.540
All because I said that...

18:34.540 --> 18:39.080
Because I relied on her so much...

18:39.080 --> 18:41.690
I wanted to show her that I could do things myself...

18:52.250 --> 18:53.780
Listen,

18:53.780 --> 18:58.600
your sister said that your words
were her one and only light.

19:00.240 --> 19:01.710
Remember,

19:02.320 --> 19:06.030
your sister was working hard all by herself.

19:06.480 --> 19:10.990
She must have been very happy to hear those words.

19:13.870 --> 19:17.750
She's telling the truth.

19:18.520 --> 19:20.290
She shared her own health with you,

19:20.750 --> 19:22.400
the one who gave her light.

19:24.610 --> 19:26.080
<i>I cast a spell!</i>

19:26.080 --> 19:28.590
<i>You only have to see me,</i>

19:28.590 --> 19:32.730
<i>and no more scary faces.</i>

19:42.610 --> 19:43.880
Nee-sama...

20:01.050 --> 20:05.420
Oscar-sama, did you just cast a spell on <i>me</i>?

20:06.410 --> 20:08.200
You noticed?

20:08.200 --> 20:10.130
You're amazing!

20:10.440 --> 20:13.890
I feel much lighter now.

20:15.210 --> 20:21.290
Do you think I would be able to cast the same spell?

20:21.290 --> 20:23.420
Yes, I'm quite sure.

20:24.830 --> 20:31.650
I'm surprised that she'd send her sister, who was so important to her, overseas.

20:31.650 --> 20:33.680
She trusts us.

20:33.680 --> 20:35.780
She trusts some strange foreigners?

20:36.270 --> 20:38.950
Japan must be full of generous people.

20:39.710 --> 20:41.080
She trusted Yune.

20:42.550 --> 20:49.720
It's the first time Yune has been interested in a far-off place.

20:58.730 --> 21:02.520
It's easy to trust something close to you.

21:03.680 --> 21:08.130
Her sister must have been very determined.

21:09.770 --> 21:11.280
What about you?

21:12.600 --> 21:17.890
You always worry about Yune coming in contact with the outside world.

21:17.890 --> 21:22.640
You said you didn't need to know more about Yune not because you trusted her,

21:22.640 --> 21:25.160
but because you were afraid to know, right?

21:25.160 --> 21:26.160
Afraid?

21:26.160 --> 21:27.430
Why would I be?

21:27.840 --> 21:33.720
The more you know, the harder
it'll be when Yune leaves.

21:40.000 --> 21:42.390
How do I look, Oscar-sama?

21:43.410 --> 21:46.440
You look a lot more like a magician now.

21:46.440 --> 21:47.190
Yeah!

21:47.440 --> 21:50.180
Time to teach you the secret spell.

21:52.160 --> 21:54.340
I'll only say this once.

21:54.340 --> 21:55.150
Okay!

22:00.910 --> 22:07.500
aa marude yume wo miteiru you na

22:00.910 --> 22:07.500
ああ　まるで夢を見ているような

22:00.910 --> 22:07.500
Ah, it's as if I'm in a dream

22:07.500 --> 22:13.300
yawarakana hikari no naka de

22:07.500 --> 22:13.300
やわらかな光の中で

22:07.500 --> 22:13.300
As I lie here in this tender light

22:13.300 --> 22:24.310
me wo tojite mimi wo sumasereba kikoete kuru

22:13.300 --> 22:24.310
目を閉じて　耳を澄ませれば　聞こえてくる

22:13.300 --> 22:24.310
When I close my eyes and listen, I can hear it

22:26.140 --> 22:39.200
atatakaku watashi wo yobu yasashii sono koe ga

22:26.140 --> 22:39.200
暖かく私を呼ぶ　優しいその声が

22:26.140 --> 22:39.200
That kind voice that warmly calls to me

22:41.790 --> 22:48.380
afureru omoi wo tsutaetai kono te kara

22:41.790 --> 22:48.380
溢れる想いを　伝えたいこの手から

22:41.790 --> 22:48.380
I want to extend my feelings with these hands

22:48.380 --> 22:54.670
kotoba ja nakute kokoro de tsunagaru

22:48.380 --> 22:54.670
言葉じゃなくて　心でつながる

22:48.380 --> 22:54.670
We connect through our hearts, not our words

22:54.670 --> 23:01.350
hajimeyou koko kara sodateyou nukumori wo

22:54.670 --> 23:01.350
始めようここから　育てようぬくもりを

22:54.670 --> 23:01.350
Let's begin here. Let's nurture the warmth

23:01.350 --> 23:07.810
atarashii hibi ga watashi wo matteru

23:01.350 --> 23:07.810
新しい日々が　私を待ってる

23:01.350 --> 23:07.810
A new day is waiting for me

23:07.810 --> 23:21.530
mamoru mono wa kitto koko ni aru no

23:07.810 --> 23:21.530
守るものは　きっとここにあるの

23:07.810 --> 23:21.530
I'm sure there is something here for me to protect

23:34.500 --> 23:35.650
Next Episode:

23:35.650 --> 23:40.980
Episode 12 :

23:35.650 --> 23:40.980
" Cats on a Roof "

23:38.830 --> 23:40.200
Please watch it.
